# Vamsa

A command-line family tree management tool. "Vamsa" (वंश) means "lineage" or "family tree" in Sanskrit.

## Features

- Store and manage family member information
- Track relationships (parent-child, spouse)
- Record important dates (birth, death, marriage)
- Export family tree data
- Backup and restore functionality

## Installation

```bash
bun install
bun run build
bun link
```

## Usage

```bash
# Add a family member
vamsa add "John Doe" --birthday 1950-01-15 --birthplace "New York"

# Add relationships
vamsa add-parent <child-id> <parent-id>
vamsa add-spouse <person-id> <spouse-id> --anniversary 1975-06-20

# View family tree
vamsa tree <person-id>

# List all members
vamsa list

# Search members
vamsa search "Doe"

# Backup data
vamsa backup

# Restore from backup
vamsa restore <backup-file>
```

## Data Storage

Data is stored in SQLite at `~/.vamsa/family.db` by default. Backups are stored in `~/.vamsa/backups/`.

